<title>UK: AHB sets 1.0 billion mark bond due July 1999.</title>
<headline>AHB sets 1.0 billion mark bond due July 1999.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers DG Bank, ABN AMRO Hoare Govett, Commerzbank, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell and Dresdner Bank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ALLGEMEINE HYPOTHEKENBANK AG</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN DEM   COUPON     3.25	MATURITY    02.JUL.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.2875   PAY DATE   S03.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.1875    LISTING    FFT	 S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> DENOMS (K) 1	   MGT/UND    0.05	SELL CONC   0.1375</p>
<p> NOTES	OEFFENTLICHE PFANDBRIEF SERIES 478</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
